==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 24~37.33 seconds<sup>720f~1,120f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
**5 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This level is practically an easier version of the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] from [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1. As such, the same strategy can be used. However, in this level, the player can wait and decide when to unleash The Face instead of him spawning at the very beginning.

Once the level has started, stall the Pigges until you have your [[Worker Cat]] at max level. Then, wait for your wallet to fill up with money, and then unleash any Cats you have on you. Again, if the player has [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat/Paris Cat]], they can use it to defeat The Face even quicker. The Pigges are also very useful for quickly getting a lot of money. After that, the player can spam Cats like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] to make quick work of The Face.

